From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:20:36 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 47/52] Plutonium: screen capture for shells, capture requests
 to the focused shell

EXO-CAPTURE (docs/features/CAPTURE.md): PlutoniumCapture, the capture
primitive. Sources are outputs (from the display list), windows (also
parked) and tabs, each with an optional region.

- navigator.windowBroker.screenshot(source) -> PNG, and
  captureCommand(): "sources", "list", "settings", "setSettings",
  "stream" (a desktop stream id for the shell's getUserMedia(): a
  MediaStream of any source, no picker), "stop", "acknowledge",
  "setSize", "answer".
- Capture requests (the portal's, over the DevTools Plutonium domain's
  captureCommand "request") go to the focused shell as a cancelable
  "capturerequest"; if it doesn't take it or goes away, Ash's own picker
  asks. Every shell gets "capturestart", "capturechange" and
  "capturestop" for every capture, and any shell can stop one. If the
  focused shell doesn't acknowledge a capture within 2 s, Ash shows its own
  indicator, with Stop buttons.
- Two global switches in local state refuse recording and screenshots.
- A capture can hold a window at a size (EmbeddedWindows::
  SetCaptureSize()), whatever its elements ask for; a captured window
  keeps drawing at full rate while parked.
- A shell's stream starts and stops with its MediaStreamUI, without
  Chrome's screen capture notification.
